      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Okshevsky et al.",
        "AbstractText": "Representatives of the genus Bacillus are common milk contaminants that cause spoilage and flavor alterations of dairy products. Bacillus sp. FMQ74 was isolated from raw milk on a Danish dairy farm. To elucidate the genomic basis of this strain's survival in the dairy industry, a high-quality draft genome was produced."
      },
